    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-8242",
      "problem": "Let $X$ be a random variable with the probability density function shown below. What are the modes of $X?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158570/assets/d63a97b931fedb6b001f590134b448dd2222f33606725343486064cec5e85036.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The modes of a random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ at the global maxima of $f(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we can tell that the global maxima of $f(x)$ are at $x=1,7,13.$\n\nTherefore, the modes of $X$ are $1,7,$ and $13.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158570/assets/f4efdc7b16747f33e48be7c73369e4f881177d6faba19d02bc832bfa0e916278.png)",
